re","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar","c":1},{"y":1568,"t":"capital_move","x":"1568: the capital is Udaipur.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar","c":3},{"y":1576,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1576: the Mughals hold Gogunda, Udaipur and Kumbhalgarh.","m":9,"cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maharana_Pratap","c":3},{"y":1585,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1585: Pratap recovers much of Mewar.","cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maharana_Pratap","c":2},{"y":1585,"t":"capital_move","x":"1585: the court is at Chawand.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar","c":3},{"y":1615,"t":"gain","x":"1615: the treaty returns Chittor.","m":2,"cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amar_Singh_I","c":2},{"y":1615,"t":"vassal_start","x":"February 1615: Mewar accepts a Mughal overlord.","m":2,"cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar","c":2},{"y":1620,"t":"capital_move","x":"1620: the capital is Udaipur again.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar","c":3},{"y":1707,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1707 (bridging): the Mughal tie lapses.","cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar","c":1},{"y":1818,"t":"vassal_start","x":"13 January 1818: Mewar accepts British supremacy.","m":1,"cp":"british-empire","cpn":"British Empire in India (East India Company rule)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar","c":3},{"y":1947,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1947: British supremacy ends.","cp":"british-empire","cpn":"British Empire in India (East India Company rule)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar","c":2},{"y":1949,"t":"dissolve","x":"1949: Mewar accedes to the Union of India.","cp":"republic-of-india","cpn":"Republic of India","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar","c":2}],"wars":[{"name":"Hammir Singh's war for Mewar","from":1326,"to":1336,"outcome":"Hammir took a base at Kelwara and, after the victory at Singoli in 1336, freed Mewar from Delhi.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_bin_Tughluq"},{"name":"Malwa-Mewar wars","from":1437,"to":1457,"outcome":"Kumbha's forces took Sultan Mahmud of Malwa prisoner in 1437; Mahmud Khalji captured Mandalgarh in October 1457.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahmud_Khalji"},{"name":"Mewar and Marwar over Mandore","from":1438,"to":1453,"outcome":"Ranmal of Marwar was killed in 1438 by Kumbha's party; Mandore passed to Mewar until Jodha retook it in 1453.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rana_Kumbha"},{"name":"Gujarat-Malwa attack on Kumbhalgarh","from":1456,"to":1456,"outcome":"'In S. 1513 (A.D. 1456) the Sultan of Gujrat \"despairing of reducing Chitor\" arrived near Abu'; Kumbha 'defeated Imad-ul-Mulk with great slaughter'; no land changed.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rana_Kumbha"},{"name":"Sanga's wars with the Lodis","from":1517,"to":1519,"outcome":"Ibrahim Lodi 'marched against Mewar in 1517' and was beaten at Khatoli, again in 1518-19 at Dholpur; no land is dated.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rana_Sanga"},{"name":"Battle of Gagron","from":1519,"to":1519,"outcome":"Sanga defeated Mahmud Khilji II and 'captured much of eastern Malwa'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rana_Sanga"},{"name":"Battle of Bayana and Khanwa","from":1527,"to":1527,"outcome":"'In the February 1527 Battle of Bayana, he defeated Babur's Mughal forces'; at Khanwa on 16 March 'the Mughals were victorious' (year inferred by the page's timeline).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rana_Sanga"},{"name":"Gujarat's sieges of Chittor","from":1532,"to":1535,"outcome":"A siege of 1533 ended with a ransom; Bahadur Shah sacked Chittor in 1535.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar"},{"name":"Siege of Chittorgarh (1567-1568)","from":1567,"to":1568,"outcome":"Akbar took Chittor and the eastern belt of Mewar.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maharana_Pratap"},{"name":"Battle of Haldighati and the Mughal occupation","from":1576,"to":1585,"outcome":"Haldighati (18 June 1576) was indecisive; Gogunda, Udaipur and Kumbhalgarh were under Mughal control from September 1576; Pratap recovered a large part of Mewar from 1585.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maharana_Pratap"},{"name":"Mughal-Mewar war under Amar Singh I","from":1606,"to":1615,"outcome":"Jahangir's armies (1606, 1608, 1609-1611) failed; Prince Khurram's campaign of 1613-1615 ended in the treaty of February 1615, which returned Chittor and the occupied lands.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amar_Singh_I"}],"certainty":[{"from":1326,"to":1949,"level":"soft","note":"No survey line is on the pages opened; Mewar's frontiers with the Rajput neighbours and the hills are approximate."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mewar","title":"Kingdom of Mewar"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rana_Kumbha","title":"Rana Kumbha"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rana_Sanga","title":"Rana Sanga"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maharana_Pratap","title":"Maharana Pratap"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amar_Singh_I","title":"Amar Singh I"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahmud_Khalji","title":"Mahmud Khalji"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_bin_Tughluq","title":"Muhammad bin Tughluq"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marwar_Kingdom","title":"Marwar Kingdom"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ranas_of_Mewar","title":"List of ranas of Mewar"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maldeo_Rathore","title":"Maldeo Rathore"}]}